* One entry of Lean's ` poolGo ` at a prefix (Steps23.lean ` poolGo_append ` , ` poolGo_single ` ): the reversed pool of the first ` j + 1 ` divisors, encoded over ` Z' ` , is ` p = d k + 1 ` pushed on that of the first ` j ` when ` p <_ x , z < p ` and ` p ` is prime, unchanged otherwise; the cost of the entry is ` pgc x z k d ` .

